{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "38", "S": "35"}}, "news": [{"title": "India office occupancy may touch 89.5% by March 2028: Report", "para": "India's office market is projected to see occupancy levels rise to 89-89.5% by March 2028. Notably, net office absorption is expected to reach around 62-64 million square feet annually during this period. Demand from Global Capability Centres will contribute 45-50% of this absorption, reflecting a shift towards higher-value functions. Vacancy rates are anticipated to decline in five major markets, enhancing overall performance.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/india-office-occupancy-may-touch-89-5-by-march-2028-report/136151965?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-281434/136151965.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "Residents in Kochi plan protest over water woes", "para": "Residents of Kochi are grappling with severe drinking water shortages, sparking protests in multiple neighborhoods. The challenges arise from a combination of leaks, aging pipelines, and insufficient infrastructure. Areas like Poonithura, Kumbalam, and Fort Kochi are particularly hard-hit. Local councillors have raised concerns, demanding that the Kerala Water Authority take urgent action. Plans for a new water treatment plant could potentially alleviate the ongoing crisis.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/residents-in-kochi-plan-protest-over-water-woes/136151825?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103/136151825.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Ten spots in Gurugram to get temporary C&D waste storage facilities: Haryana CM", "para": "Gurgaon is embarking on a significant initiative by establishing ten temporary storage sites dedicated to managing construction and demolition waste effectively. Each planned site spans one hectare and will be fortified to prevent any debris spillage. Chief Minister Nayab Singh Saini underscored the urgency for a systematic approach to waste management during a recent meeting.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ten-spots-in-gurugram-to-get-temporary-cd-waste-storage-facilities-haryana-cm/136151731?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-302396/136151731.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}